    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Thanks for figuring this out. This change might be ok for a quick-fix, but looking at the larger picture, the way the options are currently set for the shared module is a hack. There are several places in the code base that say `if Options.annotate or options.annotate`, which is a clear indication that there shouldn't be two ways to do it. We should look at the global config module's `Options.annotate` only once to set the run specific `options.annotate`, and then only use the latter. That would make it easy for the shared module to overwrite the run specific option.\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @scoder in https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/7912#issuecomment-5385896702_\r\n            ",
